<title>SOUTH KOREA: KEPCO INTERIM NET PLUNGES 66.9 PCT.</title>
<headline>KEPCO INTERIM NET PLUNGES 66.9 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	  (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				   176  vs 532</p>
<p>    Net					 110.5  vs 333.5</p>
<p>    Revenue				 5,890.4  vs 5,341.0</p>
<p>    Recurring profit			268.9  vs 433.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Korea Electric Power Corp is South Korea's exclusive supplier of electricity. The fall in profits was due to a rise in fuel costs and foreign exchange losses, a company offiical said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5643</p>
</text>
